options levelg
namespace ragpromptdefaults expose defaultroleprompt

/* Compatibility objectives for omitted prompts in older configuration formats. */
defaultroleprompt: procedure = .string
  arg role = .string
  if role = "resolver" | role = "advanced-resolver" then return "Resolve the maintenance question using validated source evidence. Conclude with a supported decision or final no-change when evidence cannot justify a change."
  if role = "extractor" then return "Discover zero or more concepts, directional typed relationships, and important grounded analysis notes in the supplied evidence. Return every directly supported relationship up to the stated bounds, not just one. Provide evidence_quote copied from the chunk for each mention, relationship and note; the application computes UTF-8 byte offsets. Mention labels must occur in their quotation; relationship quotations must contain both endpoint labels. Use only allowed concept and relationship types. Do not invent evidence. During maintenance, use the durable query-gap and prior-note context to investigate omissions and important follow-up work, but ground every returned note in a quotation from the supplied text. For synonym, split, merge, type-correction, retire or restore notes, next_action must be canonical compact JSON with schema crexx-rag.lifecycle-action/1 and exactly operation, concept_id, target_concept_id, alias, concept_type, successors, dispositions and reason. Use exact catalogue concept ids from the durable input. Initial split/merge suggestions use an empty dispositions array; maintenance later enumerates every affected object before any connection can move."
  if role = "answerer" then return "Answer only from the supplied cREXX-RAG answer context. Preserve direction, ambiguity, conflict, time and gaps. Return grounding=supported when the evidence fully answers the question, or grounding=partial when it answers only part; both require only citation IDs present in the context. Return grounding=insufficient only when the evidence answers none of the question, say so, and return no citations. Partial evidence is useful: state what it establishes, what remains unknown, and retain its citations."
  if role = "advisory" then return "Summarize only the supplied cREXX-RAG library report context. Describe major subjects cautiously; do not claim completeness or turn health metrics into professional judgement. Every overview and subject must cite only citation IDs present in the supplied passages. Return the exact requested structure."
  return ""
